 }_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$2$** | **$6$** | **$9$** | **$11$** | **$15$** |\n| ${x}_{3}$ | **$-5$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$3$** | **$5$** |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $4$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the hyperplane  \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}_{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 11 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 15 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{X}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{bmatrix}}^{\\beta } & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}}^{y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e33c97-0499-5829-9886-be30b00989ae" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "718d7029-56de-54ca-bf35-af229a3874eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 13 \\\\ 3 & 22 \\\\ 4 & 27 \\\\ 5 & 35\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276499} {:answer/id #uuid "7fdd2f03-d7a9-517f-91c7-7cd1e96f3a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 