sorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309217} {:answer/id #uuid "5c67c65c-e450-555f-b668-cccb5f1bf987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309441} {:answer/id #uuid "9a608db6-cabb-52af-bbf2-20f8e0bf5a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309992} {:answer/id #uuid "b9863cfc-9ca7-5a80-86de-fa7f88e0d12e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310255} {:answer/id #uuid "c588907a-23dc-5e04-b672-1b60d23ba8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310333} {:answer/id #uuid "e80a9562-4678-5dd7-8406-ffaa3ddd9242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9863cfc-9ca7-5a80-86de-fa7f88e0d12e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310255} :answer-field/id #uuid "593b990f-0917-5a0a-9583-6abf66430a1f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28801ee7-4094-546f-80f1-323ab0a686c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309056} {:answer/id #uuid "936148be-c895-512e-a8b4-453974a921cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309927} {:answer/id #uuid "b1417f52-3430-53a8-89df-f2088b841205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310181} {:answer/id #uuid "b950e995-a80a-5abd-92df-e7f7d0acd62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310252} {:answer/id #uuid "d97fb2d7-a4f9-51c7-9e27-fd188021b12e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310498} {:answer/id #uuid "dc5916c2-7281-5d14-af22-17ed86e13bfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28801ee7-4094-546f-80f1-323ab0a686c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309056} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8a6cb35-9607-5233-b317-7d1b4f617bba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1615e325-2155-58bc-8224-1e266a097c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308911} {:answer/id #uuid "9add62ef-516b-580e-83a4-1a29c85b07fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310000} {:answer/id #uuid "f4afa95d-fe0a-593f-bd7e-eadd38e090f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9add62ef-516b-580e-83a4-1a29c85b07fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310000} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf12da8d-9d68-5094-80cc-6cb07a044b47" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96c6b0d2-9e5e-5dae-9ba3-c5858d13dffd" :question/math-academy-id "q-335372" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)={x}^{2}+3{x}^{3},$ then $f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0.$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O({x}^{2}+3{x}^{3})$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,3{x}^{3}=O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,f=O({x}^{2})$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,{x}^{2}=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(x)$  as $x\\to 0$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O(\\underbrace{{x}^{2}+3{x}^{3}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2}+3{x}^{3}),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L2}$ we have\n\n$$\n3{x}^{3}=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L2}$ and the $\\text{absorption property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L3},$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O({x}^{2})\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand from line  $\\text{L4},$   we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L3 and L4}$ and by $\\text{the transitive property},$  we conclude that\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157454 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffe4292f-7653-5486-975e-c206acae734e" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Properties of Big-O"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "143783ba-f667-5508-b07b-b9fa079bbea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308897} {:answer/id #uuid "1c468251-7329-5d23-9077-e19b8e8726bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308967} {:answer/id #uuid "60059968-1161-56a5-a638-36fd6b700958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309471} {:answer/id #uuid "608c36e3-b013-5cae-8a3d-d4b915200e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309481} {:answer/id #uuid "